# The bridge forms of fix -bridges. A use is pointed at the target of a
# generic alias with one type parameter, a wrapper whose body is a call
# statement, and a wrapper that instantiates its target with its own type
# parameters, all or the first of them. A use is reported, with the reason,
# for a type of its own, an alias of a type literal or of an instantiation,
# a var declared with a type, a var or const that names no other package's
# declaration, a wrapper that does more than call, passes other arguments or
# other type arguments, and for an increment of or the address of a var
# bridge. A blank declaration is no bridge. git grep and the load failing
# stop it.
go build ./...
fail fix -bridges -report-only
cmpout want/plan
fail fix -bridges
cmp internal/app/app.go want/app.go
go vet ./...
failgit grep
fail fix -bridges
stderr ^pkgmove: git .*grep.*: exit status 128: fake git failure$
failgit
cp want/go.mod go.mod
fail fix -bridges
stderr ^pkgmove: type-check the importers for GOOS=linux: 
